{"timestamp":"2026-08-12T05:27:54.200Z","ordinal":52,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_019ff471-0058-7aa3-90bc-43d2cd7dac6b","call_id":"call_sjx9rSHSIiU55HcP3B7lC7YF","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"--- RESULT 1 ---\n#!/bin/zsh\nset -euo pipefail\nexport PATH=\"/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/opt/homebrew/bin\"\n\n# ===========================================================================\n#  SOCIAL MEDIA GUARD\n#  Closes the creators (YouTube + Instagram/TikTok/X/Facebook) that Matthieu\n#  chose to stop watching. Instead of a hard block, the tab switches to a\n#  countdown page: after WAIT_MINUTES a button opens the content for\n#  REWARD_MINUTES, then the tab is caught again.\n#\n#  How blocking stays fast (no visible frame of the real page):\n#    - FAST pass  (~0.1s): checks only the ACTIVE tab and redirects it inside\n#      AppleScript. Runs only while a browser is frontmost. Kills the frame.\n#    - DEEP pass  (~1s):   full sweep of every tab, resolves YouTube videos\n#      through yt-dlp, handles the reward, catches background tabs.\n#\n#  File map:\n#     1. Config              - paths, timings, browsers\n#     2. Blocked creators    - BLOCKED_PATTERNS (single editable source)\n#     3. Small helpers       - dates, text, url encoding\n#     4. Files and migration - folders, password, old names\n#     5. On / Off            - disabled, suspended, active window\n#     6. Match engine        - does this text point to a blocked creator?\n#     7. Reward (grace)      - temporary earned access, per creator\n#     8. Block page          - the HTML shown in the tab\n#     9. Browser control     - list tabs, redirect one tab\n#    10. Fast pass           - instant redirect of the active tab\n#    11. Watch loop          - the loop the background service runs\n#    12. Install             - user service (+ optional root layer)\n#    13. Commands            - status, suspend, disable/enable, uninstall\n#    14. Entry point         - command line dispatch\n#\n#  Usage: SocialMediaGuard.sh <command>\n#    install-user | status | enable | disable | suspend [min] |\n#    enforce | watch-tabs | close-tabs | uninstall-user |\n#    install-root | uninstall-root | cleanup-root\n# ===========================================================================\n\n\n# --- 1. Config -------------------------------------------------------------\n\nOWNER=\"zenray\"\nMEMORY_ROOT=\"${MEMORY_ROOT:-/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory}\"\nFOCUS_DIR=\"$MEMORY_ROOT/Focus\"\n\nSECRET_FILE=\"$FOCUS_DIR/.SocialMediaGuardPassword\"     # local password (git-ignored)\nSTATE_DIR=\"$FOCUS_DIR/.SocialMediaGuardState\"          # internal state (git-ignored)\nDISABLED_FILE=\"$STATE_DIR/disabled\"                    # present = guard turned off\nSUSPEND_FILE=\"$STATE_DIR/suspend_until\"                # epoch when suspension ends\nBLOCK_PAGE_FILE=\"$FOCUS_DIR/SocialMediaBlocked.html\"   # the page shown in the tab\nBLOCK_PAGE_URL=\"file://$BLOCK_PAGE_FILE\"\nILLUSTRATION_URL=\"file://$MEMORY_ROOT/ArtDirection/output_v3.png\"\n\n# YouTube daytime gate (separate from the creator list below): all of\n# youtube.com/youtu.be is closed during this window, every day. \"Ask for\n# time\" opens it immediately for a shrinking ladder of minutes, once per\n# click, until the ladder is spent for the day.\nYT_DAY_START_HOUR=\"${SMG_YT_START_HOUR:-10}\"\nYT_DAY_END_HOUR=\"${SMG_YT_END_HOUR:-19}\"\nYT_GRANT_MINUTES=(15 12 9 6 3)  # 5 asks/day, shrinking, 45 min total\nYT_BLOCK_PAGE_FILE=\"$FOCUS_DIR/YouTubeDaytimeBlocked.html\"\nYT_BLOCK_PAGE_URL=\"file://$YT_BLOCK_PAGE_FILE\"\nYT_DAY_FILE=\"$STATE_DIR/youtube_daytime_day\"              # YYYY-MM-DD of last reset\nYT_GRANTS_USED_FILE=\"$STATE_DIR/youtube_daytime_grants_used\"\nYT_UNTIL_FILE=\"$STATE_DIR/youtube_daytime_until\"           # epoch, current grant expiry\n\n# Timings (overridable from the plist via environment variables).\nWAIT_MINUTES=\"${SMG_WAIT_MINUTES:-30}\"      # wait before the content can open\nREWARD_MINUTES=\"${SMG_REWARD_MINUTES:-30}\"  # how long access lasts once earned\nSTART_HOUR=\"${SMG_START_HOUR:-0}\"           # active window: 0..24 = always on\nEND_HOUR=\"${SMG_END_HOUR:-24}\"\nFAST_SLEEP=\"${SMG_FAST_SLEEP:-0.1}\"         # active-tab poll interval (seconds)\nDEEP_EVERY=\"${SMG_DEEP_EVERY:-10}\"          # deep sweep once every N fast passes\n\n# Background service (LaunchAgent).\nUSER_LABEL=\"com.zenray.social-media-guard.tabs\"\nROOT_LABEL=\"com.zenray.social-media-guard\"\nUSER_PLIST=\"$HOME/Library/LaunchAgents/$USER_LABEL.plist\"\nROOT_PLIST=\"/Library/LaunchDaemons/$ROOT_LABEL.plist\"\nSCRIPT_PATH=\"$MEMORY_ROOT/Tools/FocusGuard/SocialMediaGuard.sh\"\nUSER_LOG=\"$HOME/Library/Logs/SocialMediaGuard.tabs.log\"\nUSER_ERR_LOG=\"$HOME/Library/Logs/SocialMediaGuard.tabs.err.log\"\n\n# Optional root layer (hosts + Chrome policy). Inactive without sudo.\nHOSTS_FILE=\"/etc/hosts\"\nHOSTS_MARK_START=\"# ZENRAY_SOCIAL_MEDIA_GUARD_START\"\nHOSTS_MARK_END=\"# ZENRAY_SOCIAL_MEDIA_GUARD_END\"\nCHROME_POLICY_FILE=\"/Library/Managed Preferences/com.google.Chrome.plist\"\nCHROME_POLICY_BACKUP=\"$STATE_DIR/com.google.Chrome.plist.before-guard\"\nCHROME_POLICY_MARKER=\"$STATE_DIR/chrome_policy_backup_state\"\nHOST_DOMAINS=()\nCHROME_BLOCKLIST=()\n\n# Browsers we drive. Every Chromium shares Google Chrome's tab vocabulary\n# (\"using terms from\"); Safari has its own.\nCHROMIUM_BROWSERS=(\n  \"Google Chrome\" \"Google Chrome Beta\" \"Google Chrome Canary\" \"Chromium\"\n  \"Brave Browser\" \"Brave Browser Beta\" \"Microsoft Edge\" \"Microsoft Edge Beta\"\n  \"Vivaldi\" \"Opera\" \"Opera GX\"\n)\n\n\n# --- 2. Blocked creators (single source of truth) --------------------------\n#\n# Each entry is matched as a substring, case-insensitive and separator-\n# insensitive (see Normalize), against two things:\n#   1) the tab URL (any network) - blocks YouTube, Instagram, TikTok,\n#      Facebook and X as soon as the entry is the account handle;\n#   2) the identity yt-dlp returns for a /watch page (channel name, uploader)\n#      - catches every video and side channel of a creator, even without\n#      knowing their exact handle.\n# Safety: an entry that matches nothing blocks nothing (harmless miss). So we\n# can be broad on NAMES and stay precise (joined handle or URL) to never block\n# a third party by accident.\n#\n# A few entries keep accents on purpose: they are real creator names, and a\n# channel identity like \"HugoDecrypte\" written with the accent is only caught\n# by the accented form.\n\nBLOCKED_PATTERNS=(\n  # --- Ici Japon ---\n  \"youtube.com/@icijaponcorp\"  \"youtube.com/channel/uct11zynefnunokgcrso9uyg\"  \"ici japon\"\n  # --- Silicon Carne / Carlos Diaz ---\n  \"youtube.com/@siliconcarnepod\"  \"siliconcarne\"  \"silicon carne\"  \"carlosdiaz\"  \"carlos diaz\"\n  # --- Oussama Ammar ---\n  \"youtube.com/@oussamaammaroff\"  \"youtube.com/channel/ucxh-b8b2sx4kgshsvj3ngza\"\n  \"oussamaammaroff\"  \"oussamaammar\"  \"oussama ammar\"\n  # --- Yomi Denzel ---\n  \"youtube.com/@yomidenzel\"  \"youtube.com/yomidenzel\"  \"youtube.com/channel/uchge6r4qaugajalyijoccgw\"\n  \"yomidenzel\"  \"yomi.denzel\"  \"yomi denzel\"\n  # --- Antoine Blanco (+ business channel) ---\n  \"youtube.com/@antoineblanco\"  \"youtube.com/@antoineblanco99\"  \"youtube.com/@antoineblancobusiness\"\n  \"youtube.com/channel/uc0kcckhmqfiguifkqco-iya\"  \"antoineblanco\"  \"antoine blanco\"\n  # --- Sixtine Moulle-Berteaux ---\n  \"youtube.com/@sixtinemoulleberteaux\"  \"sixtinemoulleberteaux\"  \"sixtine.moulleberteaux\"\n  \"sixtine moulle\"  \"sixtine moulle-berteaux\"\n  # --- Wallerand Moulle-Berteaux ---\n  \"wallerandmoulleberteaux\"  \"wallerand.moulleberteaux\"  \"wallerand moulle\"  \"wallerand moulle-berteaux\"\n  # --- Eric Larcheveque ---\n  \"ericlarcheveque\"  \"eric larcheveque\"  \"eric l'archeveque\"  \"eric larchevêque\"\n  # --- Guillaume Moubeche ---\n  \"guillaumemoubeche\"  \"guillaume moubeche\"  \"guillaume moubèche\"\n  # --- Alex Hitchens (+ side channels via identity) ---\n  \"alexhitchens\"  \"alex hitchens\"\n  # --- Julien Chieze (gaming news) ---\n  \"julienchieze\"  \"julien chieze\"\n  # --- HugoDecrypte (news, all channels) ---\n  \"youtube.com/@hugodecrypte\"  \"youtube.com/@hugodecrypteactus\"  \"youtube.com/@hugodecryptegrandsformats\"\n  \"hugodecrypte\"  \"hugo decrypte\"  \"hugo décrypte\"\n  # --- Le Crayon (news/media) ---\n  \"youtube.com/@lecrayon\"  \"le crayon\"\n  # --- La Chapelle Radio / Hugo Bentz ---\n  \"youtube.com/@la-chapelle-radio-hugo-bentz\"  \"la chapelle radio\"  \"hugo bentz\"\n  # --- Matthieu Stefani / Generation Do It Yourself ---\n  \"matthieu stefani\"  \"generation do it yourself\"  \"génération do it yourself\"  \"gdiy\"\n  # --- Pauline Laigneau ---\n  \"youtube.com/@paulinelaigneau\"  \"pauline laigneau\"\n  # --- Les Decouvreurs ---\n  \"youtube.com/@les_decouvreurs\"  \"les decouvreurs\"  \"les découvreurs\"\n  # --- Theophile Eliet (hyphen handle, handled by Normalize) ---\n  \"youtube.com/@theophile-eliet\"  \"theophile eliet\"  \"théophile eliet\"\n  # --- Le Precepteur ---\n  \"le precepteur\"  \"le précepteur\"\n  # --- My Better Self ---\n  \"mybetterself\"  \"my better self\"\n  # --- LouisSan (+ side channels: LouisSanCorp...) ---\n  \"louissan\"  \"louissancorp\"\n  # --- Business / make-money / mindset / manosphere sphere (NAMES only) ---\n  \"iman gadzhi\"  \"imangadzhi\"  \"andrew tate\"  \"tristan tate\"  \"cobratate\"\n  \"enzo honore\"  \"enzo honoré\"  \"franck nicolas\"  \"idriss aberkane\"  \"anthony bourbon\"\n  \"hasheur\"  \"owen simonin\"  \"lorenzo ferrante\"  \"mick levy\"  \"younes belghazi\"\n  \"yann darwin\"  \"yan darwin\"  \"raoul pop\"  \"david laroche\"  \"fabien snauwaert\"\n  \"romain pichon\"  \"tugan bara\"  \"tugan.baranovsky\"  \"morgan prevel\"  \"morgan prével\"\n  \"valentin decker\"  \"jean riviere\"  \"jean rivière\"  \"jeremy kohlmann\"  \"aurelien amacker\"  \"aurélien amacker\"\n  \"squeezie\"  \"naval ravikant\"  \"navalravikant\"  \"laurent alexandre\"  \"alexandre cicoupoulos\"\n)\n\n\n# --- 3. Small helpers ------------------------------------------------------\n\nSay()      { printf '%s\\n' \"$*\"; }\nNowEpoch() { date '+%s'; }\n\n# Drop case AND separators: \"Theophile-Eliet\", \"theophile.eliet\" and\n# \"theophile eliet\" all become \"theophileeliet\". One place that removes the\n# whole family of separator bugs (hyphen vs dot vs space).\nNormalize() {\n  local s=\"${1:l}\"\n  printf '%s' \"${s//[-._ ]/}\"\n}\n\nUrlEncode() { python3 -c 'import sys,urllib.parse;print(urllib.parse.quote(sys.argv[1], safe=\"\"))' \"$1\"; }\nUrlDecode() { python3 -c 'import sys,urllib.parse;print(urllib.parse.unquote(sys.argv[1]))'         \"$1\"; }\n\n# Value (decoded) of query parameter $2 in the URL $1.\nExtractParam() {\n  local u=\"$1\" name=\"$2\" q pair\n  q=\"${u#*\\?}\"\n  [[ \"$q\" == \"$u\" ]] && return 0          # no '?' means no query string\n  for pair in ${(s:&:)q}; do\n    [[ \"$pair\" == \"$name=\"* ]] && { UrlDecode \"${pair#$name=}\"; return 0; }\n  done\n}\n\n# Normalized form of every entry, computed ONCE at load (not inside the loop\n# that runs many times per second), to avoid needless work.\nNORMALIZED_PATTERNS=()\nfor _p in \"${BLOCKED_PATTERNS[@]}\"; do NORMALIZED_PATTERNS+=(\"$(Normalize \"$_p\")\"); done\nunset _p\n\n# The subset the fast pass uses: entries that can appear in a URL (no spaces),\n# lowercased. Spaced names never appear in a URL, so they stay for the deep\n# pass only (matched against the yt-dlp identity).\nFAST_PATTERNS=()\nfor _p in \"${BLOCKED_PATTERNS[@]}\"; do\n  [[ \"$_p\" == *\" \"* ]] && continue\n  FAST_PATTERNS+=(\"${_p:l}\")\ndone\nunset _p\n\n\n# --- 4. Files and migration ------------------------------------------------\n\n# Rename the files from older versions (YouTube*, then SocialMediaFocus*) to\n# the current names, so we keep the local password and any running reward.\n# Idempotent: after migration the old ones are gone. Never overwrites a file\n# that already exists under the new name.\nMigrateLegacy() {\n  local old\n  for old in \"$FOCUS_DIR/.SocialMediaFocusGuardPassword\" \"$FOCUS_DIR/.YouTubeFocusGuardPassword\"; do\n    [[ -f \"$old\" && ! -f \"$SECRET_FILE\" ]] && mv \"$old\" \"$SECRET_FILE\" 2>/dev/null\n  done\n  for old in \"$FOCUS_DIR/.SocialMediaFocusGuardState\" \"$FOCUS_DIR/.YouTubeFocusGuardState\"; do\n    [[ -d \"$old\" && ! -d \"$STATE_DIR\" ]] && mv \"$old\" \"$STATE_DIR\" 2>/dev/null\n  done\n  rm -f \"$FOCUS_DIR/YouTubeBlocked.html\" 2>/dev/null\n  return 0\n}\n\nEnsureDirs() {\n  MigrateLegacy\n  mkdir -p \"$FOCUS_DIR\" \"$STATE_DIR\"\n  chmod 700 \"$STATE_DIR\" 2>/dev/null || true\n}\n\n# Create a local password on first run (Matthieu does not memorize it; the\n# assistant can read it on disk if a real unlock is ever needed).\nEnsureSecret() {\n  EnsureDirs\n  EnsureBlockPage\n  EnsureYouTubeDayBlockPage\n  if [[ ! -f \"$SECRET_FILE\" ]]; then\n    umask 077\n    /opt/homebrew/bin/openssl rand -base64 48 | tr -d '\\n' > \"$SECRET_FILE\"\n    printf '\\n' >> \"$SECRET_FILE\"\n  fi\n  chmod 600 \"$SECRET_FILE\" 2>/dev/null || true\n  if [[ \"$EUID\" -eq 0 ]]; then\n    chown \"${OWNER}:staff\" \"$SECRET_FILE\" \"$FOCUS_DIR\" \"$STATE_DIR\" 2>/dev/null || true\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"--- RESULT 2 ---\n# Social Media Guard\n\nAnciennement « YouTube Focus Guard » (2026-05-21), renommé le 2026-07-09. Ne vise plus seulement YouTube mais aussi Instagram, TikTok, X/Twitter et Facebook des mêmes créateurs.\n\nBut : couper l'accès réflexe aux créateurs business / make-money / actu que Matthieu a décidé de ne plus regarder, pour tenir le cap créateur-technique (Unreal / Houdini). Barrière comportementale, pas prison cryptographique.\n\n## Mécanique : compte à rebours + récompense (pas un blocage sec)\n\nQuand un onglet pointe vers un créateur listé, il bascule sur une page locale à compte à rebours de 30 minutes.\n\n- Pendant ces 30 min : le contenu est inaccessible. Assez long pour se fermer l'onglet soi-même, ou faire autre chose d'abord.\n- Une fois les 30 min réellement écoulées : un bouton « Open now » ouvre le vrai contenu pour 30 minutes (grâce), puis l'onglet est de nouveau intercepté.\n- La grâce est scopée au créateur demandé : gagner l'accès à l'un ne débloque pas les autres.\n\nPage en anglais, ton neutre, chiffres en Anthropic Serif et texte en Anthropic Sans. Durées réglables via `SMG_WAIT_MINUTES` (défaut 30) et `SMG_REWARD_MINUTES` (défaut 30).\n\n## Couverture\n\n- Permanent, 24h/24.\n- Navigateurs : Chrome, Safari, Brave, Edge, Vivaldi, Opera, Chromium — seuls ceux réellement lancés sont pilotés.\n- Réseaux : YouTube + Instagram + TikTok + X/Twitter + Facebook, dès que le pseudo du créateur apparaît dans l'adresse.\n- Pages `/watch` YouTube : l'identité réelle de la chaîne est résolue via `yt-dlp`, donc une vidéo d'un créateur bloqué est interceptée même sans son pseudo dans l'URL (attrape aussi les chaînes secondaires).\n\n## Liste des créateurs\n\nSource unique éditable : tableau `BLOCKED_PATTERNS` en tête de `Tools/FocusGuard/SocialMediaGuard.sh`. Un motif qui ne correspond à rien ne bloque rien (échec bénin), donc on peut être large sur les noms. La comparaison ignore casse, tirets, points, underscores et espaces (« theophile-eliet » = « theophile eliet »).\n\n## Mot de passe\n\nGénéré localement dans `Focus/.SocialMediaGuardPassword`, ignoré par Git, jamais affiché dans le chat. Matthieu ne le mémorise pas ; l'assistant peut le relire localement si un vrai déblocage (suspend/disable) est nécessaire.\n\n## Commandes\n\n```bash\nGUARD=/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory/Tools/FocusGuard/SocialMediaGuard.sh\n\"$GUARD\" install-user      # installer ou recharger la surveillance d'onglets\n\"$GUARD\" status            # vérifier l'état\n\"$GUARD\" close-tabs        # forcer une passe immédiate\n\"$GUARD\" suspend 30        # suspendre 30 min (mot de passe requis)\nsudo \"$GUARD\" cleanup-root # retirer la couche réseau système, si besoin\n```\n\n## Couche root optionnelle (une seule fois, avec sudo)\n\n`install-root` ajoute une couche système : `/etc/hosts` pour les domaines purs, et une policy Chrome (`URLBlocklist` + `IncognitoModeAvailability=1`) qui désactive l'incognito Chrome — ce qui fait passer toute navigation en fenêtre normale, vue par la surveillance d'onglets. Sans cette couche, la surveillance ne voit ni les fenêtres privées / incognito, ni Firefox (limite réelle : en HTTPS le chemin d'URL n'est pas visible au niveau réseau, seul le domaine l'est).\n\n## Limite réelle\n\nUn admin Mac peut toujours démonter son propre système. L'outil est assez fort pour casser le réflexe automatique, pas pour résister à une volonté consciente de tout désactiver.\n\n## Historique des noms\n\n`YouTube Focus Guard` → `Social Media Focus Guard` → `Social Media Guard`. Le script migre automatiquement l'ancien mot de passe et l'état interne au premier lancement sous le nouveau nom.\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"--- RESULT 3 ---\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Blocked</title>\n<style>\n  @font-face { font-family:\"AnthropicSans\"; src:url(\"file:///Users/zenray/Library/Fonts/AnthropicSans-Light.ttf\") format(\"truetype\"); font-weight:300 }\n  @font-face { font-family:\"AnthropicSans\"; src:url(\"file:///Users/zenray/Library/Fonts/AnthropicSans-Medium.ttf\") format(\"truetype\"); font-weight:500 }\n  @font-face { font-family:\"AnthropicSerif\"; src:url(\"file:///Users/zenray/Library/Fonts/AnthropicSerif-Light.ttf\") format(\"truetype\"); font-weight:300 }\n  @font-face { font-family:\"AnthropicSerif\"; src:url(\"file:///Users/zenray/Library/Fonts/AnthropicSerif-Regular.ttf\") format(\"truetype\"); font-weight:40